 ## Changelog
+- `done` shader pass for the OPPO A5i video (black terrain flicker, dark leaves, no light shafts, ~6 fps). Written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain or a GPU: not compiled, not run; +1 test (`photon::deferred_shader_validates`), `vl` tests changed (`march_is_shafts_only_and_hdr` replaces `lookups_use_photons_shadow_code`). Numbers below are from the video (143 frames in 22.9 s: 160 ms average, 470 ms worst), not from a profiler:
+    - Black flicker, root cause in `render/post.wgsl` TAA: `sqrt(m1 - m0 * m0)` (variance clip) rounds to a hair below 0 on flat areas -> NaN, which the old `max0v(history)` did not clear on every driver (it came back one frame later: the strobe). Also `reinhard_inverse` divided by `1 - x` with x >= 1 after the YCoCg clip, and CAS divided 0 / 0 on a black 3x3. Now `sane()` (integer test for the all-ones exponent, survives fast-math) guards the TAA inputs, history and output and the grade input, the variance is `max(.., 0)`, the inverse is clamped to < 1, CAS divides by `max(max_color, 1e-4)`. The deferred pass guards its own decode and output the same way.
+    - Dark, flickering leaves: the surface shadow was computed in `vl.rs` at half resolution from a face normal rebuilt from the depth buffer; alpha-cut leaves have noisy depth, so the axis snap picked a wrong face and `n.L <= 0` shadowed them (the TAA jitter made it flicker). Now `photon.rs` `fs_deferred` looks the shadow up at full resolution with the G-buffer's exact face: normal offset of ~1.2 texels (x the distortion factor, more at grazing angles), a 0.15 block depth bias, 4 hardware-bilinear compares rotated by IGN, faded to `get_lightmap_shadows` at the map edge. Deleted from the march: `face_normal`, `view_pos`, the PCSS include and its blocker search (the `shadows::pcss_wgsl` code stays, unused). `Photon::new` / `draw_deferred` take the shadow group.
+    - Light shafts: their colour was AstraLex's LDR scale next to a 7x HDR sun. `Params::hdr(light_color)` replaces it with `photon::lighting().light_color * SHAFT_GAIN (0.30) * (1 - 0.8 rain)`; the time-of-day weights are unchanged. The march takes 8 samples (was 10, spacing x1.4 keeps the reach). The shadow cone can no longer black out the frame (its darkening was already capped at `SHADOW_DARK`).
+    - Cost: `RENDER_SCALE` 0.67 (`gpu/context.rs`): depth, G-buffer, HDR scene, shafts and the post chain run at the scaled size and `fs_final` upscales (bilinear taps on the output grid + CAS one source pixel apart; `Post::new` / `resize` take the surface size). `ENTITY_SHADOWS` (`lib.rs`) false: no per-frame 1024^2 entity map, no second fetch per tap. The FPS log line now prints CPU ms per frame (without the swap-chain wait): near the frame time = CPU-bound (chunk generation / meshing on the render thread), far below = GPU-bound.
+    - UNVERIFIED on a device: all of it. Levers: `RENDER_SCALE`, `SHAFT_GAIN`, `MARCH_STEPS`, the PCF radius / bias in `photon.rs`, `Settings.taa` / `cas`. ponytail: the entity cone umbra still loops up to 8 boxes per full-resolution pixel when mobs are near (`CONE_MAX`); the shadow map is still redrawn on every `mesh_gen` change while chunks stream in.
 - `done` milestone 6 of the Photon port: GTAO, water + translucent layer, weather (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +3 tests not run: `gtao::shader_text_is_complete`, `water::water_text_and_pack`, `weather::rain_columns_and_gaussian`; the last compares `JavaRandom::next_gaussian` with the JDK value for seed 42 from memory):
     - `render/gtao.rs`: `d3_ao.fsh` + `gtao.glsl` + slerp/catmull-rom/r2, half resolution, temporal accumulation, ping-pong history. Outputs `ambient` (ao, SSS, bent normal xy) and `history_data` (1 - depth, age); `AO_UPSAMPLE_WGSL` is `d4_deferred_shading`'s depth-aware upsample for milestone 1 to paste. Normal rebuilt from depth until the G-buffer exists (marked `ponytail:`). Not wired into `lib.rs`: nothing reads it yet.
     - `render/water.rs`: `gbuffers_all_translucent` water path (Gerstner waves, height variation, parallax, `get_water_displacement` in the vertex stage, texture + edge highlight, `water_fog_simple` absorption, GGX sun/moon highlight, diffuse) into a translucent layer with its own depth + a refraction target, then `c1_blend_layers` (refraction + `scene * (1 - a) + rgb`). Needs a scene colour texture that is not the target (milestone 1's HDR buffer) and a stored opaque depth. Missing, all because the input is milestone 2/3/4/5's: sky and environment reflections, PCSS shadows (uses the pack's no-shadow `pow8(skylight)`), cloud shadows, `common_fog`/analytic fog (uses the chunk shader's terrain fog), Purkinje shift. Sky/ambient colours are uniforms (`Frame`).
